Reorganised the backend around one concern per module. Each provider driver now lives in its own module under `core/drivers/`, with the shared normalisation in `core/drivers/base.py`; each REST endpoint family is a package under `core/services/` with a module per HTTP verb and its own `configure.zcml`, following the layout `plone.restapi` uses for its own services. The JWT minting the callback and the magic-link confirmation both needed is now a single helper rather than two copies. The test tree mirrors the source tree. No endpoint, registry record or public name changed. @ericof
